1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,900
Can an AI coding agent teach a robot duck new skills—and prove that they work?

2
00:00:05,900 --> 00:00:08,200
We gave Microduck three measurable challenges.

3
00:00:08,200 --> 00:00:15,800
First: spin through one full turn without falling or drifting away.
The controller completed 1.2 turns, with only four centimeters of drift.

4
00:00:15,800 --> 00:00:24,000
Next: reach two offset markers in sequence, forcing a steering reversal.
It reached both markers in 5.86 seconds and stayed upright.

5
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:32,500
Finally: approach a free ball and push it at least thirty centimeters.
The learned controller moved it one full meter.

6
00:00:32,500 --> 00:00:41,600
The key lesson is simple: keep the proven locomotion policy frozen,
then optimize a small supervisory controller above it.

7
00:00:41,600 --> 00:00:46,800
Every result has a clear pass-or-fail gate,
and the code and measurements are public on GitHub.

8
00:00:46,800 --> 00:00:50,000
This is Sarvoday Robotics. Subscribe to follow the next open robotics challenge.
